Upon reading this, I started thinking of the description of the Gates of 
Hell from _Paradise Lost_, and of the description of Hell there in 
general, which is rather more interesting than NH's Gehennom.

BTW, if you get a copy (from Project Gutenberg?), make sure it is an 
annotated one, otherwise you will have no idea what the heck is going 
on.  Milton was being deliberately awkward; contemporary writings like 
_The Pilgrim's Progress_ are still quite easy to understand today.

PS. Before you ask, I am actually an atheist outside of Nethack.

